<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">crone-of-ash</ansi>

The Crone of Ash is the elite class of the Hag (evil witch route). It needs
alignment -30 or lower at level 30. Her curses make hexed foes easier to hit
and far more fragile, and spread when they end.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Ashen Curse        hexed foes take 40% more damage, and allies have +8
                        Attack against them
  35 Rotting Miasma     Miasma's poison deals double damage
  40 Dread everywhere   Dread Whisper checks every enemy group
  45 Lingering Curse    when a hex ends, the foe stays exposed for 1 round
  50 Deeper Ashen Curse hexed foes take 55% more damage
  55 Soul Rot           a hexed foe that falls forces a morale check on its
                        group
  60 Crone's Doom       once a battle, a foe that stays hexed 3 rounds in a row
                        falls; a boss loses 10% of its health instead

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How it plays</ansi>

She hexes on her own like any witch (<ansi fg="command">help witch</ansi>). A foe counts as hexed
while it is asleep, paralyzed, poisoned, blighted, knocked down, hobbled or
exposed. Poison lasts the longest, so Miasma is the way to Crone's Doom. Each
line says what her curse did: (lingering curse, exposed), (soul rot, 3 morale
checks), (crone's doom, N damage).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Witch elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves, Iron Will, Hex Reach.
See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help witch-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help hexes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help morale</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>.
